  "claims": [
    "RootRigid is an explicit catalogue contract: any step at/inside a primitive redex is that same primitive step with the same target. It is not an assumption of arbitrary parallel-path coherence.",
    "Under RootRigid, all pairs of one-step mixed rewrites resolve either to the same step or a previously constructed separated square. Local residual routes have length at most one and guards covered by the original two step supports.",
    "Under RootRigid and an actual decreasing strategy, joinBounded constructively joins any two directed rewrite paths from a common source. Both residual path supports stay within any finite set covering the two input path supports.",
    "A complete actual step selector and natural-number rank construct an irreducible normal endpoint. Any two reachable irreducible endpoints agree as typed syntax. Normal endpoints are invariant along reachable paths.",
    "For the actual MAC catalogue, primitive sources contain two box leaves with no proper redex, and same-source roots coincide. Every rewrite removes exactly one box under arbitrary fixed sequence/tensor/wiring contexts.",
    "The executable MAC selector checks a positive untyped root pattern followed by typed reconstruction, and proves completeness. It never trusts the untyped tag alone.",
    "The MAC normalizer returns an actual directed rewrite path and irreducibility proof for every typed mixed input circuit. Its path length is bounded by the source box count, not by a runtime measurement.",
    "A finite static MAC footprint computed from source box labels contains the support of every rewrite path from that source, including all intermediate/elimination conditions introduced later.",
    "Cached conditions outside a change set plus refreshed conditions on the static footprint intersection repair normalization comparisons in the checked updated MAC model; arbitrary correlated past and complete original input can be retained in the output joint law.",
    "For chain parameter n, the input has n+1 preparation boxes and one elimination box. All n normalize to the direct elimination at index n+1 in exactly n+1 rewrites. The static guard envelope is Finset.range(n+2)."
  ],
