  "scope": [
    "Pure wiring values are fixed leaves/contexts. No new association, copy, discard, or routing rewrite is in the MAC catalogue. Do not treat this as completion of the mixed structural-and-cryptographic critical-pair basis.",
    "RootRigid is restrictive and need not hold after adding general structural or cryptographic rules. The generic result is not an unconditional theorem for arbitrary mixed catalogues.",
    "Local joins and guarded directed confluence are constructed as residual paths. A higher-dimensional cell comparing the two original proof paths, a finite complete higher presentation, and its full coherence/pasting algebra are not yet returned by this new layer.",
    "The source footprint is conservative declared metadata, not semantically minimal assumptions or a lower bound on rechecking cost.",
    "Box count bounds rewrite length only. No total generation-time, certificate-byte, condition-proof cost, Lean kernel-checking cost or native execution-time claim follows.",
    "Pairing processes distinct input components with local randomness conditional on input values. It does not implement continued native alias-preserving access through duplicated mutable oracle handles.",
    "The MAC model reuses original games, full state/trace, the same attack/query order and existing 1/256 condition. No new cryptographic security bound or general mixed-diagram security-bound contract is proved.",
    "Computational certified reductions with actual code/resources/loss transformers and the continuing native execution have not been newly interpreted in this normalization layer.",
    "The updated checked local-model contract is explicit. Its verification cost is outside the set-intersection repair claim.",
    "Ordinary shared-lemma proof generation/repair under the same assumptions has not been compared for these new normalization and confluence algorithms. No exclusive dimensional advantage or novelty priority is claimed."
  ],
